        "i ne znali": 3,
        "i povelo že": 5,
        "ne vymyla že": 2,
        "ponesla": 3,
        "vyvela že": 1,
        "i unesli": 1
      },
      "full_string": "352311",
      "advocates": ["Colleague 3", "Colleague 4"]
    },
    "Model_B_Traditional_Surface": {
      "principle": "Root/prefix types determine stress. Mobile verbs (nes-, ve-) have ending stress (-la, -lo, -li). Negation 'ne' retracts mobile stress from -lo/-li to 1. Enclitic 'že' attracts mobile stress to itself (5). Conjunction 'i' is a weak proclitic and cannot bear stress. In the absence of 'ne' or 'že', mobile forms surface with inflectional ending stress.",
      "predictions": {
        "i ne znali": 3,
        "i povelo že": 5,
        "ne vymyla že": 2,
        "ponesla": 3,
        "vyvela že": 1,
        "i unesli": 4
      },
      "full_string": "352314",
      "advocates": ["Colleague 1", "Colleague 2", "Colleague 5", "Colleague 6", "Colleague 7", "Colleague 8", "Colleague 9", "Colleague 10", "Colleague 11", "Colleague 12"]
    }
  },
  "item_status": {
    "item_1_i_ne_znali": "Unanimous: 3 (fixed root zna-)",
    "item_2_i_povelo_že": "Unanimous: 5 (mobile unaccented stem passes stress rightward to enclitic že)",
    "item_3_ne_vymyla_že": "Unanimous: 2 (dominant prefix vy-)",
    "item_4_ponesla": "Unanimous: 3 (feminine mobile past ending -la)",
    "item_5_vyvela_že": "Unanimous: 1 (dominant prefix vy-)",
    "item_6_i_unesli": "Crucial divergence: 4 vs 1. 10 colleagues support 4; 2 colleagues support 1."
  },
  "evaluation_of_item_6": {
    "arguments_for_1": "In formal linguistics problem design (Zaliznyak's Law), the system operates on binary features (+/-). All 11 examples perfectly obey: leftmost (+) wins; if no (+), initial syllable wins. Under this formal rule, 'i unesli' has only minus morphemes, so stress must fall on syllable 1 ('i'). Postulating that -li is stressed requires multiple ad-hoc rules (ne retracts from -li but not -la; že attracts from -li but not from -la or root).",
    "arguments_for_4": "Conjunction 'i' is never stressed in any given example ('i mylo' = 2, 'i vela' = 3, 'i ne unesla' = 5). In Slavic accentology, 'i' is a non-accentable clitic, while East Slavic mobile plurals end in stressed -lí ('uneslí')."
  },
  "current_lean": "While Model A (352311) is the textbook Olympiad formulation of Zaliznyak's Law, Model B (352314) holds overwhelming majority consensus (10-2). Keep close track of whether colleagues converge toward 352311 or whether the group solidifies 352314."
}

